---
source: system/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"setarch\")"
---
Run a program with altered architecture or personality flags

Usage: setarch [OPTIONS] [ARCH] [COMMAND]...

Arguments:
  [ARCH]        Architecture name, such as linux32, linux64 or i686
  [COMMAND]...  Program to run, with its arguments. Required unless --list or --show is given

Options:
      --list                  List the recognised architecture names and exit
      --show [<PERSONALITY>]  Show personality flags and exit. Without a value, shows the
                              personality of the current process, or of the one given with --pid.
                              With a value, decodes that value instead
  -p, --pid <PID>             Read the personality of process PID from /proc/PID/personality. Only
                              works together with --show
  -v, --verbose               Print what we're doing
  -R, --addr-no-randomize     Disable address-space randomisation (ADDR_NO_RANDOMIZE)
  -F, --fdpic-funcptrs        Turn on FDPIC_FUNCPTRS (function pointer-style returns)
  -Z, --mmap-page-zero        Turn on MMAP_PAGE_ZERO (map page 0 read-only)
  -L, --addr-compat-layout    Use the legacy bottom-up address layout (ADDR_COMPAT_LAYOUT)
  -X, --read-implies-exec     Make readable pages executable too (READ_IMPLIES_EXEC)
  -B, --32bit                 Cap the address space to 32 bits (ADDR_LIMIT_32BIT)
  -I, --short-inode           Return only 16-bit inode numbers from stat() (SHORT_INODE)
  -S, --whole-seconds         Round timeouts up to whole seconds (WHOLE_SECONDS)
  -T, --sticky-timeouts       Don't reduce system call timeouts when interrupted with EINTR
                              (STICKY_TIMEOUTS)
  -3, --3gb                   Cap the address space to 3GB (ADDR_LIMIT_3GB)
      --4gb                   Remove the 3GB cap, which gives the default 4GB layout
      --uname-2.6             Make uname() report kernel 2.6.x (UNAME26)
  -h, --help                  Print help
  -V, --version               Print version
